
====================================================================================================
S1. Comoving observers in FRW have EXACTLY zero four-acceleration (sympy, general a(t))
====================================================================================================
  FRW metric diag(-1, a^2, a^2, a^2);  H = a'/a = Derivative(a(t), t)/a(t)
  nonzero Christoffels (the ones that matter):
    Gamma^0_ij = a a' delta_ij  ->  Gamma^0_11 = a(t)*Derivative(a(t), t)
    Gamma^i_0j = H delta^i_j    ->  Gamma^1_01 = Derivative(a(t), t)/a(t)
    Gamma^mu_00 = [0, 0, 0, 0]   <- ALL ZERO, the crux
  [OK] comoving u is correctly normalised: u.u = -1
  four-acceleration a^mu = [0, 0, 0, 0]
  [OK] a^mu = 0 EXACTLY for comoving FRW, for arbitrary a(t) -- comoving matter is geodesic
  [OK] |a|^2 = 0, so Theorem B's first moment <Box_u>_u = |a|^2 = 0

====================================================================================================
S2. Hence Box_u u = 0 identically: u sits in the KERNEL of the operator
====================================================================================================
  Box_u u^mu = u^a grad_a ( u^b grad_b u^mu ) = u^a grad_a ( a^mu ).
  S1 gives a^mu = 0 as a VECTOR FIELD (not just at a point), so its covariant derivative
  vanishes too and Box_u u^mu = 0 identically on the background.
  By spectral calculus, if Box_u u = 0 then for any function K analytic off the spectrum
      K(Box_u/a0^2) u_mu = K(0) u_mu .
  This is not an approximation -- u is an exact zero mode of the operator on FRW.
  [OK] Box_u u = 0 identically on FRW, so K(Box_u) u reduces to K(0) u

====================================================================================================
S3. *** K(0+) = 0 AND K IS NON-ANALYTIC AT 0 -- the MI term vanishes and cannot be expanded ***
====================================================================================================
  K(z) = (sqrt(4*z + 1) - 1)/(2*sqrt(z))
  K(0+)      = 0
  series at 0: K(z) = sqrt(z)*(1 - z)   <- leading term sqrt(z), NOT analytic
  K'(0+)     = oo
  [OK] K(0+) = 0 exactly -- vanishing inertia at zero acceleration (the deep-MOND limit)
  [OK] K'(0+) diverges: K ~ sqrt(z), so K has a BRANCH POINT at the origin and no Taylor expansion exists around the cosmological background

  CONSEQUENCE, and this is the answer to channel A:
   * The MI matter term on the FRW background is
         -(1/2) rho_m s u^mu K(Box_u/a0^2) u_mu  =  -(1/2) rho_m s K(0) (u.u) = 0 ,
     because K(0) = 0. The term VANISHES IDENTICALLY on the background.
   * And because K ~ sqrt(z) at the origin, there is no analytic expansion in which to
     collect 'first-order corrections to the Friedmann equation'. The perturbative object
     the calculation was supposed to produce DOES NOT EXIST.
   * So MI contributes NO background modification and NO distance tilt. Channel A is not
     unbuilt -- it is ILL-POSED AS I POSED IT.
  numerical witness of sqrt behaviour:          z         K(z)   K(z)/sqrt(z)
                                             1e-08    1.000e-04       1.000000
                                             1e-06    1.000e-03       0.999999
                                             1e-04    9.999e-03       0.999900
                                             1e-02    9.902e-02       0.990195
  [OK] K(z)/sqrt(z) -> 1 as z -> 0, confirming the square-root branch point numerically

====================================================================================================
S4. Where MI DOES live: peculiar accelerations of real structure, against a0
====================================================================================================
  Exact FRW is the one configuration with zero acceleration. Real matter is not comoving:
  perturbations carry peculiar gravitational accelerations g ~ (4 pi/3) G rho_bar delta R.
   scale R (Mpc)   delta    g (m/s^2)   g/a0 canon   g/a0 alt       regime
             1.0    1.00    2.319e-14       0.0002     0.0002    deep MOND
            10.0    0.50    1.159e-13       0.0012     0.0010    deep MOND
            50.0    0.20    2.319e-13       0.0025     0.0021    deep MOND
           100.0    0.10    2.319e-13       0.0025     0.0021    deep MOND
           300.0    0.05    3.478e-13       0.0037     0.0031    deep MOND
  [OK] large-scale perturbations sit at g/a0 = 2.48e-04 to 3.72e-03 -- not merely below a0 but 2-4 ORDERS below it, i.e. EXTREMELY deep in the modified regime
  MI is therefore a PERTURBATION-sector effect: the background is exactly unmodified (S1-S3)
  while perturbations are as deeply modified as anything in the theory. The corpus was right
  to call the unbuilt piece the 'MI LINEAR cosmology' -- linear means PERTURBATIONS.

  *** BUT THIS EXPOSES A SECOND, UNRESOLVED INCONSISTENCY IN THE FRAMEWORK'S OWN NUMBERS ***
  If mu_fw were applied pointwise to these accelerations, inertia would be suppressed by
  mu_fw(g/a0) ~ g/a0, so the growth-driving force per unit inertial mass would be AMPLIFIED
  by 1/mu_fw ~ a0/g:
     R (Mpc)       g/a0   naive 1/mu_fw
         1.0   2.48e-04          4036.7
        10.0   1.24e-03           807.3
        50.0   2.48e-03           403.7
       100.0   2.48e-03           403.7
       300.0   3.72e-03           269.1
  So a naive pointwise reading gives growth amplification up to ~4037x, against the
  corpus's quoted flow boost of nu ~ 1.2-1.7 -- a discrepancy of 2-4 ORDERS OF MAGNITUDE.
  Something must regulate it (the cosmological external-field effect is the obvious
  candidate: every perturbation sits inside the whole universe's field), but that
  regulation is NOT DERIVED anywhere in the corpus. Until it is, nu ~ 1.2-1.7 is an
  estimate whose provenance does not survive this order-counting, and the flow-boost
  numbers that fed channel C should be treated as unfounded rather than merely uncertain.
  [OK] the naive pointwise amplification (4037x) exceeds the corpus's nu ~ 1.2-1.7 by orders of magnitude -- an unresolved gap, now on the record

====================================================================================================
S5. VERDICT on channel A, including a correction to my own framing
====================================================================================================
  SELF-CORRECTION FIRST. mi_phantom_artifact_2026.py posed channel A as 'MI modifies the
  Friedmann equation'. That framing was WRONG, and wrong for a reason visible in the action
  I had not read closely enough: the MI term is built from u^mu K(Box_u) u_mu, and comoving
  FRW makes u an exact zero mode. MI cannot modify the homogeneous background at all. The
  'right size, right regime' encouragement in that script (cH0/a0 = 7.00) was a coincidence
  of scales, not evidence of a coupling -- and I should have checked the coupling first.

  WHAT THIS SETTLES:
   1. MI produces NO background distance tilt. Not small -- structurally zero, because
      K(0) = 0 kills the term on any configuration with vanishing proper acceleration.
   2. Therefore the phantom-artifact idea is dead AT THE ROOT, not merely unbuilt. There is
      no mechanism by which modified inertia biases d_L(z) at background level, so it cannot
      fake a phantom crossing however the fit is done.
   3. The framework's expansion history comes from its FIELD CONTENT (the AeST/ghost-
      condensate dark sector, already published and CMB-fitted), not from the inertia
      modification. That is self-consistent and was the corpus's position all along.
   4. cH0/a0 = 7.00 remains a real coincidence and is still the framework's central
      motivation -- but it is NOT a coupling. Nothing in the action makes the expansion rate
      an argument of K.

  THE ONE GENUINELY NEW STRUCTURAL FINDING, which is worth more than the dead channel:
   K has a SQUARE-ROOT BRANCH POINT at z = 0, and the cosmological background sits exactly
   at z = 0. So the framework's action is NON-ANALYTIC at the configuration cosmology must
   expand around. Any future MI linear-cosmology calculation must handle that -- a naive
   'expand K to first order in perturbations' step is not available, because K'(0+) is
   infinite. This is a concrete, quantified obstacle for the perturbation calculation the
   corpus still wants, and it was not previously on the record.
   It also explains, in hindsight, why the flow-boost estimate came out as a RANGE
   (nu ~ 1.2-1.7) rather than a number: the expansion it would need does not exist.

  REMAINING TALLY for the phantom-artifact idea: mechanism NOT NOVEL, channel B closed by
  the corpus's own SN null, C closed by sign (needs a wall, we sit in a void), D/E/F/G
  closed or negligible, and A now closed structurally. THE IDEA IS FULLY CLOSED.
  Independently: BAO alone prefers evolving DE at 3.1 sigma with NO supernovae, which no
  inertia-side story was ever going to touch.
